abstract: >-
  A 35-node (21 countries + 14 regional blocs) agent-based model of the
  global food-energy system, built on the Homer-Dixon Limited-Fuse-Big-Bang
  framework, coupled through a calibrated trade network, with historical
  retrodiction against the 2008, 2010-11, 2019-20, and 2022 food-price
  crises, a scenario catalogue of historical and counterfactual
  experiments, and a policy-search layer for multi-country intervention
  optimisation.
